  "body": "Fifteen monitoring issues arrived after the November 23 publication. Twelve already had source-bound decisions and were closed individually with dated-review and publication/exclusion evidence. Three additional IDs were outside the configured arXiv category filter; their official metadata, full text and independent scope reviews are now preserved separately from the original 234-item snapshot.\n\nCanonical coverage grows from 2,456 to 2,459 without changing any existing record. The addendum recommends two inclusions for the true November 20 source window and one scientific-artifact exclusion. Formal dated review and supplement publication follow separately. SIR-Agent's unresolved scenario-count mapping remains explicit, with no unsupported numbers in its reviewed summary. Source hashes, exact quotations, original audit bytes and the previous 40-URL live publication receipt are archived.\n\nValidation: official identity/date and historical-ID reconciliation; independent quotation/hash and bilingual-summary checks; generated build and data validation; retired-name and diff checks. No paid model calls or generation tokens. The three disabled feed workflows remain disabled.\n",
